<textList name="TEXT_START_JUB">
	<text>You have arrived at the Time Distorted Sector and are met with a strange guard who seems to ignore you.</text>
	<text>Your insides twist and turn while your brain seems to spin. This sector feels strange. There is a strange guard keeping the peace but they seem to ignore you for now.</text>
    <text>You have a strange feeling of nostalgia, almost like you've been here before, only moments ago. There is a strange guard stationed here. As long as you create no trouble, they will leave you alone.</text>
</textList>
<event name="START_JUB">
	<metaVariable name="juke_SHARK" op="set" val="1"/>
	<preventQuest/>
	<beaconType id="map_icon_start" global="false">
		<color r="46" g="252" b="51" a="1"/>
	</beaconType>
	<text load="TEXT_START_JUB"/>
	<changeBackground>BACK_SECTOR_ORCHID</changeBackground>
	<playSound>lightspeed</playSound>
	<customFleet right="false" firing="true" autoDarkening="true">CUSTOM_FLEET_ORCHID</customFleet>
	<ship load="SHARK_GUARD_SHIP" hostile="false"/>
	<choice hidden="true" req="rep_comb_ORCHID" lvl="-999" max_lvl="1" max_group="0" blue="false">
		<text>Continue...</text>
		<event load="GUARD_SHARK"/>
	</choice>
	<choice hidden="true" req="rep_comb_ORCHID" lvl="2" max_lvl="999" max_group="0" blue="false">
		<text>Continue...</text>
		<event load="GUARD_ORCHID_CRIMINAL"/>
	</choice>
</event>





<event name="GUARD_SHARK">
	<text> The guard smiles and waves at you as you pass by.</text>
	<choice>
		<text>Ignore the guard.</text>
		<event>
			<text>You now have some time to do something on the ship.</text>
			<choice>
				<text>Do something onboard the ship.</text>
				<event load="STORAGE_CHECK"/>
			</choice>
			<choice>
				<text>Do nothing.</text>
				<event/>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>Contact the guard.</text>
		<event load="GUARD_SHARK_INTERACT"/>
	</choice>
	<choice>
		<text>Attack the guard.</text>
		<event>
			<text id="text_guard_attack"/>
			<ship hostile="true"/>
			<choice hidden="true">
				<text>Continue...</text>
				<event load="MORALITY_UPDATE_ORCHID_FIGHT"/>	<!-- CHANGE TO BE SHARK MORALITY -->
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
</event>

<textList name="TEXT_GUARD_SHARK_CONTACT">
<text>The guard looks at you, it feels like they're looking deep into your past. They pause, acknowledging your presence, and wait for your next move.</text>
<text>The guard speaks briefly to say hello and falls silent once again.</text>
</textList>

<event name="GUARD_SHARK_INTERACT">
	<text load="TEXT_GUARD_SHARK_CONTACT"/>
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>Request supplies.</text>
		<event load="GUARD_SHARK_REQUEST"/>
	</choice>
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>Demand supplies.</text>
		<event load="GUARD_SHARK_DEMAND"/>
	</choice>
		<choice req="weapons" lvl="5" hidden="true">
		<text>(Upg. Weapons) Threaten the guard.</text>
		<event load="GUARD_SHARK_THREATEN"/>
	</choice>
	<choice req="shark" hidden="true">
		<text>(Shark Crew) Request assistance.</text>
		<event>
			<text>Your Shark crew communicates briefly with the guard after which they agree to give some supplies.</text>
			<autoReward level="LOW">stuff</autoReward>
		</event>
	</choice>
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>Change your mind and leave the guard alone.</text>
		<event>
			<text>You apologize and end comms. The guard makes no attempts to communicate further.</text>
			<choice>
				<text>Do something onboard the ship.</text>
				<event load="STORAGE_CHECK"/>
			</choice>
			<choice>
				<text>Do nothing.</text>
				<event/>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
</event>


<eventList name="GUARD_SHARK_REQUEST">
	<event>
		<text>The guard shakes their head, signifying that they have no supplies to spare.</text>
	</event>
	<event>
		<text>The guard nods transfers over some supplies.</text>
		<autoReward level="LOW">stuff</autoReward>
	</event>
</eventList>

<eventList name="GUARD_SHARK_DEMAND">
	<event>
		<text>These guards do not seem inanately aggresive, but when you start making demands of them you can expect they're going to retaliate.</text>
		<ship hostile="true"/>
		<choice hidden="true">
			<text>Continue...</text>
			<event load="MORALITY_UPDATE_ORCHID_FIGHT"/>
		</choice>
	</event>
	<event>
		<text>The guard does not wish to fight. They give over some supplies.</text>
		<autoReward level="MED">stuff</autoReward>
		<choice hidden="true">
			<text>Continue...</text>
			<event load="MORALITY_UPDATE_ORCHID"/>
		</choice>
	</event>
</eventList>


<eventList name="GUARD_SHARK_THREATEN">
	<event>
		<text>These guards do not seem inanately aggresive, but when you start making demands of them you can expect they're going to retaliate.</text>
		<ship hostile="true"/>
		<choice hidden="true">
			<text>Continue...</text>
			<event load="MORALITY_UPDATE_ORCHID_FIGHT"/>
		</choice>
	</event>
	<event>
		<text>The guard does not wish to fight. They give over some supplies.</text>
		<autoReward level="LOW">stuff</autoReward>
		<choice hidden="true">
			<text>Continue...</text>
			<event load="MORALITY_UPDATE_ORCHID"/>
		</choice>
	</event>
	<event>
		<text>The guard does not wish to fight. They give over some supplies.</text>
		<autoReward level="LOW">stuff</autoReward>
		<choice hidden="true">
			<text>Continue...</text>
			<event load="MORALITY_UPDATE_ORCHID"/>
		</choice>
	</event>
</eventList>


<ship name="SHARK_GUARD_SHIP" auto_blueprint="SHARK_GUARD_SHIP">
	<surrender min="5" max="6" load="GUARD_SIGNAL"/>
	<destroyed load="GUARD_SHARK_DESTROY"/>
	<deadCrew load="GUARD_SHARK_DEADCREW"/>
	<crew>
		<crewMember type="shark" prop="1"/>
	</crew>
</ship>


<event name="GUARD_SHARK_DESTROY">
	<text>You have defeated the guard. Whatever might have been in their cargo has for certain been destroyed, but you can at least salvage some supplies from the ship.</text>
	<autoReward level="MED">standard</autoReward>
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>Continue...</text>
		<event load="GUARD_SHARK_FOLLOWUP"/>
	</choice>
</event>

<event name="GUARD_SHARK_DEADCREW">
	<text>You have defeated the guard. Without crew on board to stop you, you can investigate their cargo. You find a weapon to bring back to the ship, and move on to scrap their hull.</text>
	<autoReward level="MED">standard</autoReward>
	<weapon name="GIFTLIST_KERNEL"/> <!-- Change List to Shark list!! -->
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>Continue...</text>
		<event load="GUARD_SHARK_FOLLOWUP"/>
	</choice>
</event>

<ship name="SHIP_SHARK_REINFORCEMENTS" auto_blueprint="SHARK_GUARD_SHIP_GENERIC">
	<destroyed load="DESTROYED_REINFORCEMENTS"/>
	<deadCrew load="DEADCREW_REINFORCEMENTS"/>
</ship>

<event name="GUARD_SHARK_FOLLOWUP">
	<noQuestText/>
	<removeHazards/>
	<clearCustomFleet/>
	<text>By killing the guard, you have no doubt caused them to dispatch reinforcements to track you down. Watch your step as you explore the sector.</text>
	<quest event="REINFORCEMENTS_SHARK"/>
	<choice>
		<text>Do something onboard the ship.</text>
		<event load="STORAGE_CHECK"/>
	</choice>
	<choice>
		<text>Do nothing.</text>
		<event/>
	</choice>
</event>

<event name="REINFORCEMENTS_SHARK">
	<preventQuest/>
	<beaconType id="map_icon_reinforcements" global="true" req="LOOT_COMPASS">
		<color r="200" g="55" b="82" a="1"/>
		<unvisitedTooltip>An unvisited location.</unvisitedTooltip>
		<visitedTooltip>Explored location. Nothing left of interest.</visitedTooltip>
		<undiscoveredTooltip>An unvisited location.</undiscoveredTooltip>
	</beaconType>
	<text>You thought you were safe but it appears by killing the guard this ship has set out for revenge.</text>
	<ship load="SHIP_SHARK_REINFORCEMENTS" hostile="true"/>
	<environment type="PDS" target="player"/>
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>Continue...</text>
		<event load="COMBAT_CHECK"/>
	</choice>
</event>